The one-year risk is real, but it points to a fairly clean decision:

> **Do not make Renderio’s renderer, Skia packs, PIL files, LTX, Veo, Manim, Blender, or any particular video model the product. Make Pāṭala’s durable product the structured world/teaching/media representation that can compile into all of them.**

The frontier is converging surprisingly hard on this architecture. Google DeepMind is moving Veo toward reference-conditioned, camera-controllable, editable video; Genie toward persistent interactive worlds; and its July 2026 VIPE work shows that **visual prompts themselves are becoming programmable inputs to video/world models**, not merely text prompts. ([Google DeepMind][1])

The open research frontier is saying essentially the same thing even more explicitly: World Narrative Model argues professional video generation should move from probabilistic pixel sampling to an editable **4D physical narrative**, WorldDirector separates semantic trajectory orchestration from neural rendering, and LiVER makes geometry, camera and lighting explicit control variables. ([arXiv][2])

That is where I would place Pāṭala.

---

# 1. Where this is heading

I see six major convergences.

## A. “Video models” are turning into general visual/world models

Google's research trajectory is particularly instructive.

Veo 3.1 already exposes:

* reference images/“ingredients”;
* style references;
* character/object consistency;
* scene extension;
* first/last-frame control;
* camera movement controls;
* native audio.

([Google DeepMind][3])

Google's 2025 work then showed Veo performing tasks it was not explicitly trained for—segmentation, edge detection, physical reasoning, affordance understanding and visual manipulation—suggesting generative video models are developing into more general visual reasoning systems. ([Google DeepMind][4])

And the July 28, 2026 **Visual Prompt Engineering** paper goes further: automatically modifying the image supplied to a video model can improve its reasoning more effectively than text prompt engineering in some tested tasks. ([Google DeepMind][1])

Full links:

[https://deepmind.google/models/veo/](https://deepmind.google/models/veo/)

[https://deepmind.google/research/publications/203190/](https://deepmind.google/research/publications/203190/)

[https://deepmind.google/research/publications/264392/](https://deepmind.google/research/publications/264392/)

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25537](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.25537)

### Implication for Renderio

Your keyframes, diagrams and Skia outputs may become **control programs for foundation video models**.

Not obsolete.

More valuable.

Instead of:

```text
Skia
→ final video
```

think:

```text
Pāṭala semantics
→ Skia control frame / depth / mask / layout
→ video foundation model
→ cinematic result
```

That's a huge conceptual change.

