# 2. Google Genie tells us not to bet everything on traditional 3D either

Genie 3 generates persistent navigable environments at about 20–24 fps, currently 720p, with environmental consistency over minutes and promptable events. DeepMind explicitly contrasts it with explicit representations such as NeRFs and Gaussian splats: Genie maintains its “world” through a generative model rather than requiring a traditional geometric scene representation. ([Google DeepMind][5])

Full links:

[https://deepmind.google/blog/genie-3-a-new-frontier-for-world-models/](https://deepmind.google/blog/genie-3-a-new-frontier-for-world-models/)

[https://deepmind.google/models/genie/](https://deepmind.google/models/genie/)

So I would **not** build Pāṭala around:

```text
everything must become Blender geometry
```

either.

Because in one year the output backend might equally be:

```text
WorldSpec
→ Genie-like model
```

rather than:

```text
WorldSpec
→ Blender
→ Cycles
```

The durable thing is **WorldSpec**.

