# 3. World Narrative Model is probably the most important paper for Renderio architecture

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.31946](https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.31946)

Project:

[https://glassroom.sjtu.edu.cn/WNM/](https://glassroom.sjtu.edu.cn/WNM/)

Their thesis is almost exactly the direction I would give Renderio:

```text
not:

prompt
→ diffusion
→ random pixels


but:

structured physical narrative
→ explicit 4D previsualization
→ neural renderer
```

Their representation includes:

* scene geometry;
* object layouts;
* character/animal skeleton motion;
* object trajectories;
* camera trajectories;
* lighting;
* temporal state.

Then existing video generators are treated almost like **neural shaders**. ([arXiv][2])

This is the architectural idea to steal.

Not necessarily their software.

