# 4. WorldDirector shows the same architecture with working code

This one has inference code and model weights available now:

[https://github.com/pPetrichor/WorldDirector](https://github.com/pPetrichor/WorldDirector)

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02517](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.02517)

WorldDirector has an LLM generate explicit 3D trajectories for objects **and the camera**. Those become control signals for a causal video generator; the system also maintains dynamic object identity when entities leave the view and later return. ([GitHub][6])

The example plan is JSON.

That is particularly relevant.

They're essentially doing:

```text
LLM
 ↓
WorldPlan.json
 ↓
3D object trajectories
camera trajectories
appearance bindings
 ↓
video model
```

Pāṭala should have an analogous object, but far richer semantically.

