## EmbodiedGen V2

This is even more strategically interesting:

[https://github.com/HorizonRobotics/EmbodiedGen](https://github.com/HorizonRobotics/EmbodiedGen)

Paper:

[https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.07459](https://arxiv.org/abs/2607.07459)

It doesn't merely generate meshes.

It builds **simulation-ready assets and scenes**, and has a backend abstraction where 3D generation can come from SAM3D, TRELLIS or Hunyuan3D. It packages geometry, collision proxies, physical properties and exports to multiple simulators. ([GitHub][12])

Their architecture is exactly the software-engineering lesson for you:

```text
semantic task
      ↓
stable intermediate representation
      ↓
pluggable backend:
  TRELLIS
  SAM3D
  Hunyuan
  future model
```

Do that for Renderio.

