# 13. Use OpenUSD rather than inventing your own 3D scene format

This is one area where I definitely wouldn't reinvent things.

OpenUSD's entire reason for existence is exactly what you need: composing geometry, shading, lighting, animation and assets into scenes/shots/worlds while allowing non-destructive overrides and interchange across tools. ([OpenUSD][17])

Official docs:

[https://openusd.org/release/](https://openusd.org/release/)

[https://openusd.org/release/intro.html](https://openusd.org/release/intro.html)

And use glTF/GLB for lightweight reusable runtime assets. glTF is an ISO-standardized runtime 3D asset delivery format supporting scenes, nodes, cameras, meshes, materials, skins and animation. ([The Khronos Group][18])

Official:

[https://www.khronos.org/gltf/](https://www.khronos.org/gltf/)

[https://registry.khronos.org/glTF/](https://registry.khronos.org/glTF/)

So:

```text
Pāṭala semantic IR
       │
       ▼
VisualWorldSpec
       │
       ├── USD   complex scenes / shots
       └── GLB   portable assets
```

Do not make:

```text
patala-3d-format.json
```

