## The strategic answer

Don't abandon Skia. Don't abandon the Platinum corpus. Don't spend the next year polishing them into a giant closed ecosystem either.

**Your Skia/anatomy/math/cymatics library becomes Pāṭala's deterministic visual language.**

**OpenUSD/glTF become the explicit spatial asset layer.**

**TRELLIS/SAGE/EmbodiedGen become replaceable 3D suppliers.**

**Veo/LTX/Wan/world models become replaceable neural renderers.**

**Renderio becomes the compiler/director and evaluation system.**

And **Pāṭala owns the one thing these frontier labs generally do not have: a canonical, evidence-bearing semantic model of what the generated media is actually allowed to mean.**

That architecture has a much better chance of becoming *more useful* as video/world models improve rather than being obsoleted by them.

Because this frontier is changing almost weekly, I can monitor the world-model / agentic-video / 3D-generation literature and flag only releases that materially change this architecture.

